LIST [options]

Without any arguments, LIST shows all channels visible to you.
Secret channels (+s) are hidden unless you are allowed to see them.

The list is shown in the form:

  <#channel> <number of users> :[modes] [topic]

To filter the result, pass one or more options separated by commas (',').
Recognized options are:

  *mask*   List channels matching *mask*
  !*mask*  List channels NOT matching *mask*

  <num     Show only channels with less than <num> users
  >num     Show only channels with more than <num> users

  C<num    Show channels created within the last <num> minutes
  C>num    Show channels created more than <num> minutes ago

  T<num    Show channels whose topics were changed within the last
           <num> minutes
  T>num    Show channels whose topics are older than <num> minutes

  T:mask   Show channels whose topics match the given mask

To stop a running LIST request, use the LIST command again.

See also: JOIN
